-# ns3-mmwave fork for ns-O-RAN
+# ns3-oran: AI-Driven Traffic Steering for 5G mmWave/LTE Dual Connectivity
 
-================================
+This repository contains the simulation source code developed as part of a Master's degree project, built upon the [ns3-mmwave](https://github.com/nyuwireless-unipd/ns3-mmwave) module and integrated with the [ns3-o-ran-e2](https://github.com/o-ran-sc/sim-ns3-o-ran-e2) interface.
 
-This repository is a fork of the [ns3-mmwave project](https://github.com/nyuwireless-unipd/ns3-mmwave) with updates to make it work with the [ns3-o-ran-e2](https://github.com/o-ran-sc/sim-ns3-o-ran-e2) ns-3 module.
+The core of this work is an **AI-driven Traffic Steering solution using a Multi-Armed Bandit (MAB) agent** to optimize Quality of Service (QoS) in a Dual Connectivity (LTE + 5G mmWave) environment.
 
-This module enables the support for running multiple terminations of an O-RAN-compliant E2 interface inside the simulation process. It has been developed as part of a collaborative effort between the [Institute for the Wireless Internet of Things (WIoT)](https://wiot.northeastern.edu) at Northeastern University, Mavenir, and the University of Padova.
+## Overview of the Master's Work (`scratch/scenario-master.cc`)
 
-## How to use
+The primary simulation script for this research is located at `scratch/scenario-master.cc`. It implements a sophisticated, closed-loop control system that dynamically adjusts traffic routing between LTE and mmWave base stations based on real-time network conditions.
 
-Please refer to this [quick start guide](TODO).
+### Key Features and Contributions
 
-## References
+*   **Multi-Armed Bandit (MAB) Traffic Steering:**
+    *   A centralized reinforcement learning agent continuously monitors UE throughput and adjusts the LTE/mmWave traffic split ratio (PDCP split) for eMBB traffic.
+    *   The agent's reward function is designed to prioritize QoS satisfaction (target throughput) across different traffic classes.
+*   **Mixed Traffic Profiling (eMBB and XR):**
+    *   Simulates multiple traffic types simultaneously.
+    *   **XR (Extended Reality) Traffic:** Mapped to QCI 80 (low latency) and strictly routed through the high-bandwidth 5G mmWave link.
+    *   **eMBB Traffic:** Mapped to QCI 2 and dynamically split across LTE and 5G mmWave paths based on the MAB agent's decisions.
+*   **Dynamic Traffic Scenarios (Non-Stationary Regimes):**
+    *   **`Static`:** Constant offered load throughout the simulation.
+    *   **`Step`:** Deterministic changes in the offered load at specific intervals to test the MAB's adaptability.
+    *   **`Robustness`:** Randomized, non-repeating fluctuations in eMBB and XR data rates (using Fisher-Yates shuffle) to evaluate the robustness of the MAB agent against unpredictable traffic shifts.
+*   **O-RAN Integration via Redis:**
+    *   The simulation actively pushes QoS targets (`target_mbb`, `target_xr`) and state information to a local Redis instance (`127.0.0.1:6379`).
+    *   This allows external O-RAN xApps to read the network configuration and thresholds in real-time, bridging the gap between ns-3 simulations and O-RAN RIC implementations.
 
-More information can be found in the paper
